\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Zephaniah
\toc1 Zephaniah
\toc2 Zephaniah
\mt1 Zephaniah
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The message from Yahweh which came to Zephaniah son of Ethiopia, son of Gedalyah, son of Amaryah, son of Hezekiah in the time of Amon’s son, King Josiah of Judah
\s1 Coming judgement against Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 2 Yahweh declares:
\m I will exterminate everything \add that lives\add* on the ground.
\p
\v 3 Yahweh declares:
\m I’ll bring humans and animals to an end, along with the birds and fish. Wicked \add people\add* will be destroyed along with their idols and humankind will be cut-off from the earth.
\v 4 I will punish \add the people of\add* Judah,
\q1 and those living in Jerusalem.
\q1 I will wipe all remnants of Baal out from this place.
\q1 No one will even remember the names of those priests who served idols.
\q1
\v 5 I’ll punish those who bowed down to the stars and planets from their rooftops,
\q1 and those making promises to Yahweh but then promising to \add the false god\add* Malkam.\f + \fr 1:5 \ft A variant of the name of the pagan god ‘Molech’ (or ‘Molech’, but also close to the Hebrew word for ‘king’ as found in some other translations).\f*
\q1
\v 6 I’ll punish those who turn back after following \add me,\add* Yahweh,
\q1 as well as those who haven’t searched for Yahweh or prayed to me.
\b
\q1
\v 7 Be silent in the presence of the master Yahweh,
\q2 because his day is near.
\q1 Yahweh has prepared a sacrifice,
\q2 and he’s consecrated his guests.
\p
\v 8 On the day of Yahweh’s sacrifice, I will visit their officials and the king’s sons, and all those wearing foreign clothing.
\v 9 At that time I will punish all the officials who force their way into people’s homes—the ones filling their masters’ houses using fraud and violence.
\p
\v 10 Yahweh declares:
\q1 On that day a cry of distress will come from the Fish gate,
\q1 and wailing from the second district
\q2 and a loud crash from the hills.
\q1
\v 11 Wail, \add you\add* inhabitants of the Maktesh,
\q1 because all of the people of Canaan will be destroyed.
\q1 All the money-counters will be eliminated.
\q1
\v 12 I will search Jerusalem with lamps at that time,
\q1 and I will punish those who’ve sunk to the bottom—
\q1 the ones who tell themselves,
\q2 ‘Yahweh will never take action—either good or bad.’
\b
\q1
\v 13 Their wealth will be taken as plunder
\q1 and their houses will be ruined.
\q1 They’ll build houses, but they won’t get to live in them.
\q1 They’ll plant vineyards, but won’t get to drink their wine.
\b
\q1
\v 14 Yahweh’s big day \add of judgement\add* is near—
\q2 close and coming quickly.
\q1 The sound of Yahweh’s day is bitter—
\q2 \add even\add* warriors will cry out.
\q1
\v 15 That day will be a day of anger,
\q1 a day of distress and anguish,
\q1 a day of destruction and desolation,
\q1 a day of darkness and gloom,
\q1 a day of cloud and thick darkness,
\q1
\v 16 a day of trumpet \add blasts\add* and \add with the\add* battle cry
\q1 against the fortified cities and against the high \add towers on\add* their corners.
\b
\q1
\v 17 I’ll bring distress to the people,
\q1 and they’ll walk slowly as if they were blind,
\q1 because they’ve sinned against Yahweh.
\q1 Their blood will be poured out like dust,
\q1 and their innards like dung.
\b
\q1
\v 18 Their silver, and even their gold, won’t be able to save them
\q2 on the day of Yahweh’s anger.
\q1 The whole earth will be consumed in the fire of his jealousy
\q1 because he’ll soon destroy people from all over the world.
\c 2
\s1 Do what is right
\s4 Southern kingdom
\q1
\v 1 Gather yourselves together,
\q1 \add yes,\add* assemble \add now\add* you shameless nation
\q1
\v 2 before the decree is made,
\q1 before the day passes like chaff,
\q1 before Yahweh’s anger reaches you all,
\q1 \add yes,\add* before that day of Yahweh’s anger hits you.
\q1
\v 3 Search for Yahweh, all you humble people who do his justice.
\q1 Aim to do what is right and to stay humble.
\q1 Perhaps you’ll be hidden \add away\add* on the day Yahweh’s anger.
\s1 The demolition of places near Israel
\q1
\v 4 Because Gaza will become abandoned,
\q2 and Ashkelon will become a ruin.
\q1 \add The people of\add* Ashdod will be driven out by noon,
\q2 and Ekron will be overthrown.
\q1
\v 5 The inhabitants of the coastal region are to be pitied,
\q2 the nation of the Kereti.
\q1 Yahweh’s decision is against you all,
\q2 Canaan, land of the Philistines.
\q1 I’ll destroy you until no one remains.
\q1
\v 6 The coastal region will become pastures of meadows for shepherds
\q2 and pens for flocks.
\q1
\v 7 The remaining survivors from Judah will \add inhabit\add* that region.
\q1 They will shepherd \add their flocks\add* on that land.
\q1 They’ll lie down in their houses in Ashkelon in the evening,
\q1 because their god Yahweh will visit them, and he’ll restore their fortune.
\b
\q1
\v 8 I’ve heard Moab’s mocking
\q1 and the Ammonites’ insults.
\q1 They’ve insulted my people
\q1 and built up their forces against their border.
\p
\v 9 Commander-in-chief Yahweh, Israel’s god, declares:
\q1 As certain as I’m alive,
\q1 Moab will become like Sodom,
\q1 and the Ammonites like Gomorrah,
\q1 overrun by nettles and salt-pits—in ruins forever.
\q1 The remnant of my people will plunder them,
\q1 and the remainder of my nation will take possession of them.
\q1
\v 10 That will be the fruit of their pride,
\q1 because they mocked and talked themselves up
\q1 against the people of Commander-in-chief Yahweh.
\q1
\v 11 The people of Moab and Amon will be very scared when Yahweh punishes them.
\q1 He’ll do that so powerfully that people will stop worshipping all other gods.
\q1 People in every nation will worship Yahweh instead—each person in their own country.
\b
\q1
\v 12 Also you, \add Ethiopians\add* Ethiopians), will be killed by my sword.
\b
\q1
\v 13 Yahweh will punish those in the north.
\q1 Yes, he’ll destroy Assyria.
\q1 He’ll turn Nineveh into ruins—
\q2 \add it’ll become\add* a dry place like the desert.
\q1
\v 14 Herds of every kind \add of wild animals\add* will lie down in the middle of it,
\q1 Various kinds of owls will sit on the pillars \add still standing\add*.
\q1 A call will hoot in the window.
\q1 Rubble will blocking any doorways \add still upright\add*,
\q2 because the cedar \add planks\add* will be exposed.
\q1
\v 15 This is the proud city where \add people\add* lived in security.
\q1 The one with a reputation: “No other city compares with me.”
\q1 How it’s become a ruin—a home for the wild animals.
\q1 Every one passing by will hiss at it \add in derision\add*,
\q1 \add and\add* shake their fist \add remembering their hate for it\add*.
\c 3
\s1 Jerusalem’s sin
\s4 Southern kingdom
\q1
\v 1 The one rebelling and being defiled is to be pitied—
\q2 the city of oppressors.
\q1
\v 2 She doesn’t listen to what she’s told.
\q1 She doesn’t take correction.
\q1 She refuses to trust in Yahweh.
\q1 She won’t approach her god.
\q1
\v 3 Her leaders are roaring lions among the flock.
\q1 Her judges are wolves \add that approach in\add* the evening.
\q1 There’s nothing left to eat by the morning.
\q1
\v 4 Her prophets are insolent, treacherous men.
\q1 Her priests profane the sanctuary—they violate God’s law.
\q1
\v 5 Yahweh behaves fairly in the city.
\q1 He doesn’t do anything that’s wrong.
\q1 He makes fair and just judgements every morning.
\q1 At \add every\add* dawn, he’s present there,
\q1 ^and yet those who are disobedient have no shame.
\b
\q1
\v 6 I’ve destroyed nations—broken down their walls.
\q1 I’ve destroyed their streets and now they’re deserted.
\q1 Their cities are ruined, lifeless,
\q1 without anyone living \add in them\add*.
\q1
\v 7 I said, ‘Surely you will respect me and accept correction.
\q1 Then she won’t die as a city because of my punishing her.’
\q1 ^Nevertheless, they got up early to do all their corrupt activities.
\b
\p
\v 8 Yahweh declares:
\q1 Wait for me, for when I pounce on the prey,
\q1 because my decision is to gather nations and assemble kingdoms,
\q1 to pour my indignation and all my anger out on them,
\q1 because the whole world will be consumed by the fire of my jealousy.
\b
\q1
\v 9 Then I’ll be sure to give pure speech to the peoples,
\q1 →so all of them can pray to Yahweh,
\q1 and serve him side-by-side.
\q1
\v 10 From across the rivers of \add Ethiopia\add* Ethiopia), my worshippers,
\q1 my scattered children \add will return and\add* bring my offering.
\q1
\v 11 On that day you won’t feel ashamed about all the times you disobeyed me,
\q1 because at that time, I’ll remove those proud people from among you,
\q1 and you won’t continue to be arrogant on my sacred mountain.
\q1
\v 12 And I’ll leave the poorer and humble people among you,
\q1 and they’ll trust in Yahweh’s authority.
\q1
\v 13 The surviving Israelites won’t do what is wrong.
\q1 They won’t tell lies or deceive others.
\q1 ^Instead they’ll eat and sleep in peace,
\q1 No one will be there to terrify them.
\q1
\s1 The song of happiness
\s4 Both kingdoms
\q1
\v 14 Zion’s daughter, sing happily.
\q1 All Israel, shout aloud.
\q1 Daughters of Jerusalem, be happy and triumphant will all your being.
\q1
\v 15 Yahweh will stop punishing you.
\q1 He’s forced your enemy to retreat.
\q1 Israel’s king, Yahweh, is among you.
\q1 Don’t worry any more about being harmed.
\q1
\v 16 In that day Jerusalem will be told,
\q1 “Don’t be afraid, Zion.
\q1 Don’t let your hands grow weak.
\q1
\v 17 Your god Yahweh is right there.
\q1 A powerful warrior, he’ll save you.
\q1 He’ll be so happy about you.
\q1 He’ll be silent in his love.
\q1 He’ll \add talk\add* happily about your rescue.”
\q1
\v 18 I will gather those among you who grieve so they can attend the celebrations.
\q1 They were taken as tribute and it was a reproach.
\q1
\v 19 Look, I’ll be dealing with all of your oppressors at that time.
\q1 I’ll save \add your\add* people who are disabled or who’ve been shamed.
\q1 Then I’ll get them praising,
\q1 and change their shame into a good reputation around the world.
\q1
\v 20 At that time I will bring you all in—
\q1 yes, I’ll gather you all together at that time.
\q1 You’ll have a good reputation and people all over the world will praise you,
\q1 as I restore your \add good\add* fortune right in front of your eyes.
\m Yahweh has spoken.
